WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.208
This example shows an unnormalized appointment
record

00:00:05.055 --> 00:00:08.252
The row contains patient information provider
information

00:00:08.436 --> 00:00:11.239
appointment time a comma-separated list of service

00:00:11.265 --> 00:00:13.305
codes and a matching list of charges

00:00:15.043 --> 00:00:19.517
That design creates several problems A foreign

00:00:19.531 --> 00:00:22.031
key cannot easily validate each service code

00:00:22.057 --> 00:00:25.665
inside a comma-separated list Joining to one

00:00:25.691 --> 00:00:28.994
service is difficult The charges can become

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.178
misaligned with the service codes The row

00:00:32.191 --> 00:00:37.284
also mixes several different subjects Before
normalizing

00:00:37.442 --> 00:00:39.442
state the problem clearly one row is

00:00:39.469 --> 00:00:41.508
trying to represent an appointment and several

00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:45.366
service occurrences at the same time The

00:00:45.393 --> 00:00:48.406
first normalization step will separate those
repeated

00:00:48.432 --> 00:00:50.735
service values into individual rows
